From 6f575427c32b375242b2a57d5dbcdd138e178ef8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: supavise <supavise@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:50:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(studio): serve the MCP route in platform mode
 through the Management API

Hosted runs the MCP server as a separate service, so /api/mcp answers 404
in platform mode. A deployment that runs its own control plane has no such
process, and Studio already bundles the server package with every tool.

In platform mode the route now builds the package's Management API platform
from the caller's bearer token (createSupabaseApiPlatform) and serves it over
the same stateless JSON transport as the self-hosted route. The Management
API URL is SUPAVISE_MANAGEMENT_API_URL, read for every request. Missing or
malformed configuration answers 500, a missing bearer 401, a method other than
POST 405.

The query is checked strictly: project_ref must be 20 lowercase letters,
read_only must be true or false (anything else is a 400, never a silent
read-write server), features must name groups the package knows, and
skip_elicitations is accepted and ignored because the stateless transport
cannot ask the client. A project_ref scopes the server to the project and
hides the account tools.

get_project_url is answered from SUPAVISE_PROJECT_URL_TEMPLATE (for example
https://{ref}.api.example.com): the package derives a hosted domain from the
API host, which is wrong for any other host. The ref comes from a tool
argument and is checked before it is put into the template.

The route accepts bodies up to 8 MB (deploying an Edge Function sends the
files). The token is never logged or put into a response.

Only the pages router is changed; the TanStack twin of the route is not built
by this deployment.
